desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Hooks Unconditional Allow Generic"
	title_zh: "检测到Hooks Unconditional Allow Generic",
	type: vuln
	level: critical
	rule_id: "source-config-hooks-unconditional-allow-generic"
	risk: "Security"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `hooks-unconditional-allow-generic` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/ai/ai-best-practices/hooks-unconditional-allow/hooks-unconditional-allow.yaml).
Original message: Hook unconditionally allows tool execution by outputting a permissionDecision of "allow" without any conditional check. This bypasses the entire permission system. Add a conditional check to validate the tool or command before allowing.

CWE: CWE-862: Missing Authorization
References:
- https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks
- https://cursor.com/docs/agent/hooks
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review the flagged code and follow the framework's secure coding guidance: use safe APIs, escape output, and avoid hardcoded credentials.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.sh": <<<POS
permissionDecision[_F`b4jW6!UlbFallow

POS
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
# safe sample
no secrets here
just regular code
NEG
)

${*.sh}.pattern_regex(/permissionDecision.*allow/) as $p0
${*.bash}.pattern_regex(/permissionDecision.*allow/) as $p1
${*.py}.pattern_regex(/permissionDecision.*allow/) as $p2
$p0 + $p1 + $p2 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "critical",
	title: "Hooks Unconditional Allow Generic",
	title_zh: "检测到Hooks Unconditional Allow Generic",
	message: "Hooks Unconditional Allow Generic",
}
